        <title type="html"><![CDATA[CVE-2026-31431: how Copy Fail behaves in Kubernetes]]></title>
        <id>https://www.stream.security/post/cve-2026-31431-how-copy-fail-behaves-in-kubernetes</id>
        <link href="https://www.stream.security/post/cve-2026-31431-how-copy-fail-behaves-in-kubernetes"/>
        <updated>2026-05-04T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img alt="" loading="lazy" id="w-node-_2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63771-83c22e73" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f860665de29c4a7933a962_5.png" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f860665de29c4a7933a962_5-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f860665de29c4a7933a962_5-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f860665de29c4a7933a962_5-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f860665de29c4a7933a962_5.png 1200w" class="post-image"><div class="post-content-div"><div class="div-block-992"><div class="div-block-1010"><div fs-list-field="category" class="blog-category">Cloud Security</div><div class="highlight-tag pop w-condition-invisible">Popular</div><div class="highlight-tag w-condition-invisible">Highlights</div><div class="hide w-dyn-list"><div class="w-dyn-empty"><div>No items found.</div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775_instance-4" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265dbcab8c88303f083c22dc7%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%2269f85694fb0a700ca9e0993c%22%7D%5D" href="/post/cve-2026-31431-how-copy-fail-behaves-in-kubernetes" class="b-title w-inline-block"><h2 fs-list-field="title" class="heading-29 blog">CVE-2026-31431: how Copy Fail behaves in Kubernetes</h2><div class="blog-par limit-char">A critical Linux kernel vulnerability (CVE-2026-31431, "Copy Fail") allows an unprivileged process to corrupt any file's in-memory copy without writing to disk. In Kubernetes, this means an attacker in one pod can inject malicious code into binaries used by other pods on the same node - without any special permissions, without container escape, and without leaving a trace on the filesystem. We validated this on a live EKS cluster and built runtime detection for it.</div></a></div><div class="divider-full space small"></div><div class="div-block-773"><div class="writer-small dark"><img height="70" width="70" alt="Petr Zuzanov" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png" sizes="70px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png 1400w" class="writer-image-small"><div><div fs-list-field="author" class="writer---blog-page-home">Petr Zuzanov</div></div></div><div class="div-block-790 xs w-condition-invisible"><div class="div-block-953"><div class="writer---blog-page-home date">May 4, 2026</div></div><div class="code-embed-3 w-embed"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
